                    },
                    "message": "Yes the OEM infra code that is merged does not have any issue. I had this MR part of old design which we don't need now."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Needs work at a design level.  We can't remove optmizations for large values just because it's inconvenient for plugins.  If we're parsing a json value twice, that's a bug in the plugin framework."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "I was not aware that the optimisations are intended ones and readJson API is expected to remove stuff from the input object. \nOEM infra or route handlers don't need this change. \nI created this MR from one of our previous discussion where we wanted to make the input JSON object to the read API as const reference. \nSorry the misleading commit message which was stale and part of old OEM design."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/json_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 147,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This was an intentional optimization to not make copies of large string objects.\n\nHow can we avoid removing this?"
                },
